  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual material of the police officer spilling coffee",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the police officer (police_officer) in the act of spilling coffee and shouting, as this is the central comedic and ironic subject of the meme. The user identifies with the officer's exaggerated reaction, imagining themselves in a similar situation — a mundane mishap being humorously labeled as a serious emergency. This projection is implicit, not explicit (e.g., no 'me' or 'you' text), but is inferred from the user's engagement with the meme's humor and relatability. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'police_officer'.",
